DESCRIPTION >
    Multitouch live pageview row-pull for getMultiTouchAttributionLive (the linear / time_decay /
    u_shaped / w_shaped models). Faithful 1:1 port of the pvSql at
    api/lib/attribution-engine.js:1733-1765 (queryName 'multitouch_pageviews_live').

    REPLACES THE DEAD-HogQL LEG. With PostHog frozen (Jul 9) the HogQL pageviews returned nothing,
    pageviewsByVisitor became {}, and every conversion fell to the :1866 "no pageviews -> 100%
    Direct" branch — so four of five attribution models silently credited 100% Direct in prod
    (correct revenue, fabricated source breakdown). This restores real touchpoints.

    POSITIONAL output — 23 base columns in the EXACT order the consumer destructures (row[0]..row[22],
    :1776-1798):
      distinct_id, timestamp, utm_source, utm_medium, utm_campaign, referrer, ai_source, gclid,
      gbraid, wbraid, fbclid, msclkid, ttclid, li_fat_id, li_fatid, twclid, dclid, snapclid, pclid,
      sccid, ko_click_id, page_url, utm_term
    followed by 0-2 dynamic custom columns consumed at row[23]/row[24] (:1829-1830). The seam maps
    these NAMED rows back to positional arrays (attribution-engine.js) — a wrong key renders as
    garbage and fails nowhere, so the order above is load-bearing.

    Typed-column translation (SCOPE_v3 §2.6): properties.site_id -> site_id, event -> event_type.
    NULLIF TRAP — DELIBERATELY NOT WRAPPED: all 23 base fields are Nullable(String) typed columns
    (events.datasource), so they return NULL for a missing value, matching the HogQL bag NULL
    exactly. They are selected RAW — no COALESCE/toString, which would coerce NULL -> '' and make
    derived_source (:1823) pick 'direct' for a real source. The '' -> 'direct' bug does not bite
    because the columns are Nullable, not DEFAULT-backed.

    CUSTOM COLUMNS: the live code appends `properties.custom_<key> AS custom_<key>` for the 1-2 keys
    the active groupBy/groupBy2 request (:1728-1731). Reproduced with the custom_key1/custom_key2
    {% if defined %} pattern (mirrors session_report_pageviews.pipe); the caller passes the FULL bag
    key (e.g. 'custom_plan'), read via nullIf(JSONExtractString(properties, {{ custom_key1 }}), '')
    to match the HogQL bag NULL for a missing custom property.

    Half-open window (timestamp >= lookback AND timestamp < to), ORDER BY timestamp ASC, LIMIT 100000
    — byte-for-byte with :1759-1764.

    TWO PARAM TRAPS, both proven live (curl against the deployed pipe; --check caught NEITHER):
    (#10) OPTIONAL params must carry a DEFAULT, not required=True: custom_key1/custom_key2 are only
    requested for a custom_param groupBy. {{ String(custom_key1, required=True) }} inside a
    {% if defined %} block still 400s on every call that omits it. Fixed -> {{ String(custom_key1, '') }}.
    (#11) RESERVED PARAM NAMES: the date-bound params were named `lookback` and `to`. `to` is a
    reserved token in Tinybird's template engine — it never binds, renders as __no_value__, and
    surfaces as "Required parameter is not defined. Check the parameters site_id, lookback and to"
    (Tinybird lists ALL required params when one fails, misdirecting). Proof: session_report_pageviews
    — identical {% if defined %}/DateTime structure — SERVES 69 rows with date_from_ts/date_to_ts;
    this pipe 400'd with lookback/to at the same site + same datetime value. No serving pipe uses
    `to`/`lookback`. Renamed to date_from_ts/date_to_ts (the serving convention); the seam
    (attribution-engine.js _mtParams) passes the new names. site_id/date_from_ts/date_to_ts are
    required=True — the seam always passes them (same as the serving first_touch_by_site.pipe).
    THE GATE is the curl (200 + rows, custom keys omitted), NOT `tb --cloud deploy --check` (it
    injects __no_value__ placeholders and reported "valid" on both broken versions). Founder deploys
    + adds to TINYBIRD_READ_PIPES.

NODE multitouch_pageviews_live_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        distinct_id,
        timestamp,
        utm_source,
        utm_medium,
        utm_campaign,
        referrer,
        ai_source,
        gclid,
        gbraid,
        wbraid,
        fbclid,
        msclkid,
        ttclid,
        li_fat_id,
        li_fatid,
        twclid,
        dclid,
        snapclid,
        pclid,
        sccid,
        ko_click_id,
        page_url,
        utm_term
        {% if defined(custom_key1) %}, nullIf(JSONExtractString(properties, {{ String(custom_key1, '') }}), '') AS custom_key1{% end %}
        {% if defined(custom_key2) %}, nullIf(JSONExtractString(properties, {{ String(custom_key2, '') }}), '') AS custom_key2{% end %}
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND event_type = '$pageview'
      AND timestamp >= {{ DateTime(date_from_ts, required=True) }}
      AND timestamp < {{ DateTime(date_to_ts, required=True) }}
    ORDER BY timestamp ASC
    LIMIT 100000

TYPE endpoint
